# {{full_name}}

An [Animus](https://github.com/launchapp-dev/animus-cli) provider backend for **{{name}}**.

> **Status:** Under construction — scaffolded from
> [`animus-plugin-template`](https://github.com/launchapp-dev/animus-plugin-template).
> Implement the stubbed methods in `src/backend.rs` and ship.

## What this is

A standalone stdio plugin that exposes the {{name}} inference API as an
Animus provider. The Animus agent runner dispatches `agent/run` calls
into this binary and receives streaming output, tool calls, and a final
aggregated result envelope.

## Install

```bash
animus plugin install {{org}}/{{full_name}}
```

## Configure

```bash
export {{NAME_UPPER}}_API_KEY="<your-api-key>"
# Optional overrides.
export {{NAME_UPPER}}_API_URL="https://api.{{name}}.example/v1"
export {{NAME_UPPER}}_DEFAULT_MODEL="{{name}}-large"
```

Then wire the provider into a workflow or agent profile:

```yaml
# .animus/workflows/standard.yaml
providers:
  {{name}}:
    plugin: {{full_name}}
    config:
      api_key_env: {{NAME_UPPER}}_API_KEY

agents:
  default:
    provider: {{name}}
    model: {{name}}-large
```

## Run

```bash
animus daemon start
animus workflow run --task-id <id>
```

## Roadmap

The scaffold leaves two `todo!()` bodies in `src/backend.rs`. Implement
them in this order:

- [ ] `ProviderBackend::start` — translate `SessionRequest` into the
      upstream chat-completion payload, open the streaming response, and
      yield `SessionEvent`s as tokens / tool calls arrive.
- [ ] `ProviderBackend::cancel` — abort in-flight requests via the
      upstream cancel endpoint (or by dropping the stream).
- [ ] Resume support — when `start` is called with `resume_session`,
      look up the prior message history before issuing the next turn.
- [ ] Contract tests against mocked streaming responses.
- [ ] Release binaries via the bundled GitHub Actions workflow.

